From fcb4e3dbb82b8759b329a6ea043297612973b428 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:53:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 82/87] fix(websocket): survive wrongly typed messages, one log
 subscription per connection, drop stalled readers

- handle_message caught only json::parse_error. Valid JSON of the wrong shape
  ([], null, {"type":0}, a numeric token) threw type_error out of the
  libwebsockets callback and terminated lemond, before authentication on
  /spans/stream. Non-objects are refused and any exception from a message is
  answered with an error.
- Each logs.subscribe added a LogStreamHub subscriber and kept only the newest
  id, so repeats multiplied every log line and outlived the connection (and,
  holding this, the server after a WebSocket restart). A repeat now replaces
  the connection's subscription.
- The outbound queues had no bound. A connection that stops reading is closed
  once 16 MiB is queued for it.

These are upstream code paths; the gateway exposes them on the LAN.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
